WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:02.102
Tonight, another Putin critic jailed.

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:02.769
This time

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.371
it's a former Russian police officer

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:06.539
sentenced to seven years in prison.

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:08.341
What, for seven years in prison,

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:08.808
you may ask?

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:09.309
Well,

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:10.443
the crime is criticizing

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:11.177
the war in Ukraine.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:11.678
Two friends

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.980
in a private phone conversation.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.782
So how did Russian authorities

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:16.883
find out about the conversation?

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:17.984
Just put aside the seven year

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:19.319
prison sentence right now.

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.287
They wiretap his phone.

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:22.355
Well, this development coming

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:22.756
as Russia's

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:23.456
top diplomat,

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:24.457
the foreign minister, Sergei

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.593
Lavrov, has just landed in New York City.

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:28.595
Lavrov is allowed in the United States

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:29.295
because he's here

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:30.563
for a United Nations meeting.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.899
And Russia, as ironic as it may be.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:34.901
Currently holds the rotating presidency

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.236
of the Security Council.

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:37.804
Ukraine's top top diplomat

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:40.106
called that, quote, the worst joke ever.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.341
And Lavrov today,

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.242
when he got the microphone,

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:48.481
used it to warn of a widening war.

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.749
As during the Cold War,

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:51.751
we have reached the dangerous, possibly

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.553
even more dangerous threshold.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.056
OUTFRONT now, the U.S.

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:58.024
ambassador to the United Nations,

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:59.526
Linda Thomas-Greenfield.

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:00.093
And Ambassador,

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:01.161
I really appreciate your time

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:02.195
and it's great to see you.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.830
So you were there today

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.332
with Sergei Lavrov, and I

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:07.667
curious what your reaction

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:08.701
was being in that room

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.904
and what it's like to be in the same room

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:11.805
with him now.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:14.207
You know, it was the

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.577
epitome of irony and hypocrisy

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:20.580
to have the foreign

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.849
minister of Russia

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.718
chairing the Security Council,

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.255
a meeting on multilateralism.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:32.959
Multilateralism, when Russia

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.963
has in there unilateral,

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:38.798
unprovoked action

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:42.135
against Ukraine, attacked everything

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:43.203
that the U.N.

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:46.706
charter stands for and everything

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:48.875
that we value as members

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.176
of the United Nations.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:52.278
So I held up the charter

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.047
and I read parts of the charter

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:58.151
to remind him of what that charter means.

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:00.453
And every single member of the council

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.355
talked about their support

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.289
for the charter.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:05.458
So he was really out of place

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.559
there today.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:09.129
Do you have any sense as to

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:11.431
and obviously he's been longtime

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:12.232
foreign minister, right.

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:13.333
He's dealt with negotiations

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:15.201
with John Kerry on on things.

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:16.703
Right. Over the years.

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:20.340
Do you think that he is all in?

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:21.908
Is there any part of him that gets it or.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:22.509
No?

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:25.512
I can't speak for for him.

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:28.081
But I hope that listening

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:30.783
to the members of the council today

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:32.752
that he got something

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:33.887
and what he got

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.855
was from the secretary general

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:38.024
to almost every single member

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:39.692
of the council

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.761
supporting the values

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:42.962
that underpinned the U.N.

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:45.331
Charter and criticizing Russia's

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:47.167
attack on Ukraine's

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:49.202
sovereignty and their independence.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.837
So I mentioned that police officer.

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.305
Right. Seven years in prison. Right.

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:52.906
For criticizing

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:54.007
the war in a private phone conversation,

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:54.908
they tap his phone.

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:55.875
We obviously know

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.343
about the father, right, of a girl

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.012
who had painted a Ukrainian flag

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:01.114
in school. Right. He's in prison.

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:02.715
She's in an orphanage. Right.

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:03.950
And these examples,

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.152
there are more and more and more of them.

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:07.820
There are also Americans

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.656
held in penal colonies

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:11.124
and prisons in Russia right now.

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:11.824
Elizabeth Wieland

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:12.825
is the sister of one of them,

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:13.826
Paul Wieland.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.129
He is wrongfully imprisoned.

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:17.530
He's been there for years.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.065
You introduced her to the U.N. today.

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:20.066
So she was there,

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:22.468
she spoke and Lavrov was in the room.

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:24.237
She said

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:25.238
you said you wanted him

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:26.005
to look into her eyes,

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:26.973
to see the suffering. Right.

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:27.874
That she's going through. Right.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.342
With the loss of her brother.

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:32.178
She told CNN that Lavrov did look at her.

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:33.846
You asked him to do so

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.114
and that he actually did.

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:35.848
We don't have video of it.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.750
But she said that that happened.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:38.885
What do you make of that?

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:40.820
That he would actually do that?

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.823
You know, I think he felt the pressure.

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:45.992
I didn't see him.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.460
Look, I was concentrating.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:47.994
You were delivering

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:50.363
your comment, my statement.

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:52.932
But I do know that when I turned to him

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:53.800
and said

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:56.336
you should look in her into her eyes,

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:58.371
he was pretending to read.

00:03:58.371 --> 00:04:02.909
And he did look up and so I am pleased

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:05.945
that she saw him look at her

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.581
so that he could feel her pain

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:12.619
and he can feel her suffering, not having

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:15.255
seen her brother for nearly four years.

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.889
And she also mentioned

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:17.624
the jailed Wall Street

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:18.224
Journal reporter

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:18.825
Evan Garcia,

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:20.994
which we've heard a lot about him

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:24.330
there, charging him with high rate,

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:26.165
high crimes of espionage.

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:27.867
And there

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:28.268
is, from

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:28.735
what we

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:30.670
understand, from talking to lawyers

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.105
involved and sources,

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:34.040
there's no imminent resolution to this

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.541
and they're not looking for one.

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:36.542
Do you have any idea

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.344
whether there is anything, anyone,

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.847
anything specific that Putin wants

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:42.482
for Mr. Herskovitz, his return?

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:42.782
You know,

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:46.853
what Putin wants is to use American

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:50.189
individuals, private citizens

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:53.626
as political and diplomatic pawns in

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:56.629
his aggression against Ukraine.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.832
He has not specifically said,

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:02.402
I want to trade this or trade that.

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:05.738
But he what he wants to do is use them

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:08.775
as possible

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:10.410
trades for whatever it is

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.512
he may be trying to achieve.

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:13.579
And we're doing everything

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:14.881
possible, Aaron,

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:18.451
to get all American citizens, to get Evan

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:23.823
to get Paul released from the terror

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.725
that they are experiencing

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:27.960
being in these penal colonies.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:28.561
I want

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:29.929
I want to ask you about Sudan

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:30.630
before we go.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:31.030
We've learned

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.231
there's a three day cease fire,

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:33.266
but obviously you've got a country

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:34.233
on the brink of civil war.

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:34.500
U.S.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.402
Embassy evacuated by Special Forces,

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:37.804
SEAL Team six.

00:05:37.804 --> 00:05:39.172
You know, it sort of hearkens back.

00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:40.506
I remember covering so much

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:41.307
what happened in Tripoli.

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:42.809
Right. And the horrors there.

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:44.310
Right. The death of an ambassador.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.812
So they have been evacuated,

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:48.147
but we understand there's about 16,000.

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:49.215
This is the State Department

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:50.483
or officials estimate,

00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:52.518
of how many Americans remain in Sudan.

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:53.052
Are you committed

00:05:53.052 --> 00:05:54.120
to getting all of them out

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.089
or at this point, it's sort of

00:05:56.089 --> 00:05:57.156
if you're out, you're out

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:58.224
and if you're not.

00:05:58.224 --> 00:06:00.159
You know, we we've made clear

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:01.728
we've been making clear for months

00:06:01.728 --> 00:06:02.595
that Americans

00:06:02.595 --> 00:06:06.366
should not be traveling to Sudan.

00:06:06.366 --> 00:06:08.868
And we've encouraged Americans to leave

00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:11.237
before this incident happened.

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:13.206
But we are working

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:14.941
with the United Nations

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:17.343
and supporting those Americans

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:20.680
who have expressed the desire to leave.

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:22.448
We provided some overhead

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:24.183
support to the U.N.

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:26.953
convoy that included American citizens.

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:30.189
And we have put some resources

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:31.457
to support

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:33.626
American citizens leaving Sudan.

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:36.829
And during this three day cease fire,

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:38.931
which we hope holds,

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:39.832
we encourage

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:43.369
Americans to do what is necessary

00:06:43.603 --> 00:06:46.773
to ensure that they remain in a safe

00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:48.741
and a safe position.

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:48.908
Right.

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:49.242
Of course,

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:50.309
you can't force people to do it

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:52.378
as the 16,000 people is a lot of people.

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:53.413
Ambassador, thank you very much.

00:06:53.413 --> 00:06:54.881
I appreciate your time tonight.

00:06:54.881 --> 00:06:55.948
Thank you very much.

